FlashInfer 0.7.0.post1: skip the rollback snapshot for in-place MLA metadata

Source: kindlingai/glm-5.3-flash-gx10 (Kindling) at c748079,
  experimental/fixes/_fa_common.py, by Matt Mastracci (no LICENSE file;
  used with the owner's permission). The original removed every snapshot;
  this version skips the snapshot and the copy only for a source that is
  exactly its reserved target, and keeps the rollback for real copies.
License: FlashInfer is Apache-2.0.
Upstream: not in flashinfer v0.7.0.post1.
Purpose: with use_cuda_graph=True, plan() clones every reserved metadata
  buffer before copying the new metadata in, so a failed copy can be rolled
  back. vLLM's SM90 sparse MLA backend fills kv_indices in place and passes
  the reserved buffer's own prefix, so each plan() cloned and self-copied up
  to num_tokens x top-k int32 (Kindling measured 136 MB per decode step on
  GB10). A same-storage copy is the identity, so it needs neither.

--- a/flashinfer/mla/_batch_mla/_backends/_fa_common.py
+++ b/flashinfer/mla/_batch_mla/_backends/_fa_common.py
@@ -267,6 +267,15 @@
                 (self._kv_indices_buf[: len(kv_indices)], kv_indices),
                 (self._kv_len_arr_buf, kv_len_arr),
             )
+            # A source that is exactly its reserved target (the caller filled
+            # the reserved buffer in place) needs no copy, so no rollback
+            # snapshot either. Cloning it cost a full kv_indices copy per plan
+            # (over 100 MB for sparse MLA at top-k 2048).
+            targets = tuple(
+                (target, source)
+                for target, source in targets
+                if self._storage_interval(target) != self._storage_interval(source)
+            )
             snapshots = tuple(target.clone() for target, _ in targets)
             try:
                 for target, source in targets:
